= The Pedagogical Missions

Not everything the Republic does is fought over. Into the poorest villages of Spain - places that had never seen a cinema, a library, or a reproduction of a Velázquez - go the Pedagogical Missions: travelling libraries, gramophones, film screenings, and a student theatre company, "La Barraca," directed by a young poet named Federico García Lorca, playing the classics of the Spanish stage on carts in the plaza.

Thousands of new schools are built, teachers' salaries raised, a war on illiteracy declared. This is the Republic the <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> believes in - not only bread, but books; not only the union hall, but the enlightenment of a whole people long kept in the dark.

[? if democratization >= 3 : For a moment, in the lamplight of a village schoolroom, the Republic is exactly what its founders dreamed. ?]
